LANGUAGE English

BOOK OpenPortal ORDERED NO KEEP LOOPED
    IF goal != goalOpenPortal THEN EXIT

    // this hides the page since we are NO KEEP
    // this is easier than managing visibility
    MARK Step2Repeat READ
	MARL Step5Repeat READ
	
    PAGE Step1
        PROLOG "
			{c:WhateverUncleDavid} stands at the alter, arms raised, speaking
			a language you cannot understand. You can see on the altar the
			various tools and materials needed for the ritual.
			
			The boy is chained to the floor, quietly begging his father to
			stop. 
			
            If you have the {c:QItemRitualKnife}, the
			{c:QItemRitualComponents}, and the {c:QItemElderSign}, you can
			begin to disrupt the ritual.
        
            Only {c:EventChosenInvestigator} can perform this task and only
            while standing at the altar, in the space next to {UncleDavid}.
        
            Are you ready?
        "

        BUTTON "Speak the words"

        TEXT "
			When you get closer to the altar, you see that {} does not have the
			{c:QItemElderSign}. That means he will need blook to keep the
			portal open. You must stop him before he uses you to feed it.
			
			You think back to the counterspell you memorized earlier. You hold
			the {c:QItemRitualKnife} and chalice above your head and speak the
			words. {c:UncleDavid} snaps his head toward you, as though seeing
			you here for the first time. Your eyes lock and you see a 
			determined but haunted look in his eyes.
			
			He looks back at the altar and tries to start again. Nothing comes
			out of his mouth and he looks back at you.
			
			This step is complete.
        "
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step2
        PROLOG "
            {c:UncleDavid} lowers his eyes to the dagger he holds. While no
			sound comes out, you see him moving his lips.
        "

        BUTTON "Stab {c:MonsterUncleDavid}"

        TEXT "
			You choose your moment and lunge at him with your knife. At the
			last moment, he steps to the left and your glances off of his arm
			without doing any damage.
			
			You think you can turn and make a more direct hit. Test {agility}.
			
			For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
        "
		
		// even if we pass, we fail
        TEST QUOTA 10
            ON PASS DO NOTHING
            ON FAIL DO NOTHING
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step3
        PROLOG "
			He steps away again and you stumble, bumping into him and knocking
			the {c:QItemRitualDagger} from his hand. It clatters onto the altar
			while you step back.
        "

		BUTTON "Speak the words"

        TEXT "
			{c:MonsterUncleDavid} grabs the knife and begins speaking the
			incantation again, his voice booming with power. The knife begins
			glowing and lightly, slowly pulsing.
			
			You speak the words again. Test {will}.
			
			For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
        "

        // even if we pass, we fail
		TEST QUOTA 10
            ON PASS GOTO Step3Fail
            ON FAIL GOTO Step3Fail
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step3Fail
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            You fumble the words and nothing happenes. {c:MonsterUncleDavid}
			ignores you and slides the blade across his palm.
        
            Suffer 2 Horror ({will} negates).
			
			You must stop him.
        "

        MARK Step3Repeat UNREAD
    END PAGE

	PAGE Step3Repeat
		PROLOG "
			You raise your arms again.
		"
		
		BUTTON "Speak the words"
		
		TEXT "
			You begin speaking, hoping to block his voice again. Test {will}.
			
			For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
		"
		
		TEST 4
			ON PASS DO NOTHING
			ON FAIL GOTO Step3Fail
	END PAGE


    PAGE Step4
        PROLOG "
            As {c:MonsterUncleDavid} squeeze blood from his fist into the
			chalice, the spell takes hold and he loses his voice again.
        "

        BUTTON "Make your move"

        TEXT "
			With {c:MonsterUncleDavid} distracted and frustrated, you reach
			to the altar to grab the skull. If you can only reach it before
			he... does something.
			
			Test {agility}.
			
			For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
       "
   
       // even if we pass, we fail
	   TEST QUOTA 10
            ON PASS DO NOTHING
            ON FAIL DO NOTHING
    END PAGE


	PAGE Step5
		PROLOG "
			
		"
		
		BUTTON ""
		
		TEXT "
		"
	END PAGE
    PAGE Step5
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        PROLOG "
            You can feel something happen inside but it is not very strong.
			Your uncle's lips stop moving and for a moment the worlds grows
			quiet.
			
			
			The
			portal sputters for a moment, but nothing more. You>ll have to try
			the incantation again.

            Suffer 1 facedown Damage and 1 facedown Horror ({will} negates).

            The ritual is wearing you down.
        "

        MARK Step4Repeat UNREAD
    END PAGE



    PAGE Step5
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        PROLOG "
            You grab the skull and look up at your fellow investigators with
			excitement. They are engaged with townsfolk in robes and aren>t
			able to look up.
			
			{c:MonsterUncleDavid} looks angry as he turns to face you. This
			time he does not look down. His unblinking eyes meet and hold yours
			and his mouth begins moving again.
			"
    
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step4Fail
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            You can feel something happen inside but it is not very strong. The
			portal sputters for a moment, but nothing more. You>ll have to try
			the incantation again.

            Suffer 1 facedown Damage and 1 facedown Horror ({will} negates).

            The ritual is wearing you down.
        "

        MARK Step4Repeat UNREAD
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step4Repeat
        PROLOG "
            The portal is still humming and pulsing with energy. Whatever is
            approaching is getting closer.
        
            You look at the incantation again and take a deep, calming breath.
        "

        BUTTON "Try again"

        TEXT "
            Your fellow investigators are struggling to keep you alive and one
            looks over at you and you meet their eyes. Terror. Horror.  You
			must get this. You look back down at the text.
        
            If you understand it, test {lore}; otherwise, test {will} and hope
			for the best.
        "
        
		// even if we pass, we fail
		TEST QUOTA 2
            ON PASS GOTO Step4Fail
            ON FAIL GOTO Step4Fail
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step5
        PROLOG "
            You turn the page and see the next step: you>ll need more blood. You
            have to cut yourself again with the {c:QItemRitualDagger} and let the
            blood drip on to the {c:QItemElderSign}. The book says that the blood
            will empower the {c:QItemElderSign} to completely close the portal,
			and seal this ley line in a way that will prevent another portal
			from opening here ever again.
    
            You look at your hand and see that it has stopped bleeding. Cutting
            yourself again will take courage.
        "

        BUTTON "Draw more blood"

        TEXT "
            You draw your knife across your palm again and a searing pain
            momentarily overwhelms you. You have to do this.

            You look back down at the book and speak.

            If you understand the text, test {lore}; otherwise, test {will} and
            hope for the best.
        
            For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
        "

        // even if we pass, we fail
		TEST QUOTA 10
            ON PASS GOTO Step5Fail
            ON FAIL GOTO Step5Fail
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step5Pass
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            You squeeze your hand into a tight fist over the trinket. As your
			blood drips, the it begins to glow. Then it and the knife begin
			pulsing. When you look up, you see the portal is dimmer and
			smaller, pulsing in sync with the {QItemRitualDagger} and the
			{c:QItemElderSign}. The boy screams again, no longer sounding
			human.

            The {c:QItemElderSign} rises and hovers over the altar. It vibrates
            briefly, then slowly moves across the room toward the portal.

            The boy screams one last time as the elder sign makes contact with
			his forehead. The boy goes rigid, then the portal collapses and the
			boy falls to the ground... still smoldering... still moaning.
        
            This investigation is over.
        "
		
        result = fullWin
        GOTO EventGameOverStart
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step5Fail
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            You finish the incantation, but the {c:QItemElderSign} just lies
			there. You>ll have to try again.

            Suffer 1 facedown Horror ({will} negates).
        "

        MARK Step5Repeat UNREAD
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step5Repeat
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        PROLOG "
            You lift your hand over the altar again and prepare to speak again.
            The boy is still screaming in pain and terror.
        "

        BUTTON "Try again"

        TEXT "
            You sqeeze more blood out of your fist on to the {c:QItemElderSign}.
            As it hits the trinket, the boy stops screaming.

            Test {lore} or {will}.
        
            For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
        "

        TEST QUOTA 4
            ON PASS GOTO Step5Pass
            ON FAIL GOTO Step5Fail
    END PAGE

END BOOK